From c858932d8c6824d2b39211afb5a89f3693314780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:52:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/37] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: use identity domain for SM6150
 MDSS

The SM6150 display controller can be left scanning out a splash buffer
by firmware. Attaching it to an empty translated domain before the
display driver takes over interrupts that scanout and can leave the DSI
command-mode pipeline in a persistent FIFO-underflow state.

Select the identity default domain for SM6150 MDSS, as is already done
for the other Qualcomm MDSS generations with the same firmware handoff
requirement. The MSM DRM driver will replace it with its private paging
domain during KMS initialization.

This also keeps the firmware framebuffer accessible continuously until
native DRM is ready.

Signed-off-by: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 795e8ec7e..0a6d45d75 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -421,6 +421,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-mss-pil" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6150-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6350-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mdss" },
